::JOUR_U03_L08_GP_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.NEWS.01] Source: The student newspaper is preparing a package about a new school recycling initiative. Source notes show that labeled bins will be placed near the cafeteria, gym, and library. The environmental club adviser says the goal is to reduce contamination, which happens when non-recyclable items are mixed with recyclable materials. A student volunteer says concise signs will help students sort items quickly. The editorial board is considering an opinion piece arguing that the school should also add a short recycling reminder to morning announcements. The package needs a factual news brief, a feature angle, an editorial claim with evidence and rebuttal, clear revision, publication conventions, vocabulary support, and a short oral briefing. Question 1: Which response best matches the Unit 3 task? {
